You can check this by typing "import win32api" and "import win32con" at 
the python prompt (they should 'do nothing' with no error messages).

> The second question is when you installed R, did it update the registry? 
> This is an option at install time (defaults to true I think).

 From the R-project FAQ for Windows:
 >> After installation you can add the Registry entries in
 >> HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE by running RSetReg.exe in the bin folder, and
 >> remove them by running this with argument /U. Note that this 
requires >> administrative privileges and neither sets up nor removes 
the file
 >> associations.

